  '**More features without leaving your app**
- Dictionary lookups, word details, and the full Anki card editor now open in a floating window over the game instead of switching apps. Deck selection, card type and field mapping, and the audio picker all live there too.
- Language pickers and the audio-source picker (TTS voices, Commons recordings, game audio) moved into the same window.

**Anki**
- New global text-to-speech speed slider that also applies to audio saved into cards.
- Big cards no longer fail with "make sure AnkiDroid is running". Oversized cards are detected up front and offered simplified instead of silently dying.
- Hold-to-create word cards and sentence-mode Definition fields now use full styled dictionary formatting.
- Controller hold-A sends a card like a held finger press, and the capture sheet closes when you do.
- Smaller fixes: the "already in Anki" pip renders on styled panels, the remove button is easier to hit, and the audio picker shows the current selection on open.

**Dictionaries and lookups**
- Several common word families were missing from the shipped packs. Fixed and updated.
- Japanese: suffix taps work again (づらい, にくい, やすい, だらけ, 向け, 済み and others), compound words split correctly, usually-kana words display and save as kana, and mistaken readings-based splits are gone.
- Imported (Yomitan) dictionaries are found for inflected words and kana spellings, render styled everywhere, and no longer flash unstyled first.
- 押して resolves to 押す · Te-form instead of the fossilized adverb (work by [danillogical](https://github.com/danillogical))

**Translation**
- Claude is available as a translation backend preset. Unfortunately, it only works with usage credits and not monthly membership.
- New on-device Hy-MT2 translation model, available in the EU, UK, and South Korea.
- Errors are honest: rate limits, server errors, and quota problems no longer all read as "Offline", and services recover as soon as the network comes back instead of staying sidelined.

**Capture and overlays**
- Greatly reduced noise for Paddle OCR
- Fixed a crash on some devices when using on-device translation models.
- The status bar and navigation pill no longer pop up over immersive games when an overlay takes focus.
- Fixed a firmware-triggered device restart on the AYN Thor, a magnifier lens that could freeze on screen, and a dead-end home screen on single-screen devices.
- Floating icon polish: a clearer state indicator, a much smaller touch target on the intro animation, and per-cell cues for what opens a detail page.',
