    ('v3.1.1', 'v3.1.1', '### New in 3.1.1

- **Fixed magnifier lens preview word** A 3.1.0 regression left the drag lens stuck on "Find a word" for every Latin-script language, Korean and Thai: no word label while you dragged, and holding in place never opened the definition.
- **Multi-word expressions in the lookup popup.** Tap any word inside a known expression and the popup splits in two: the whole expression on top, the single word below, each with its own entry and its own tap into full details. "a great deal", "give up", "il y a" and "máy tính" are now reachable from any of their words, including the leading "a", and the single-word lookup is never taken away from you. Same for Japanese from the other side: phrases like 気になる, 手当たり次第 or 放送番組 now shows the dictionary words that make it up.

## What''s new in 3.1.0

- **Anki cards new UI and editable.** Note types are built from real fields instead of one HTML blob, so you can edit cards in AnkiDroid and map any field onto your own note type. The Word and Sentence templates were redesigned: structured sense lists, pitch-accent tooltips, frequency ratings, your accent colour, and tap-a-word-to-jump-to-its-row on sentence backs.
- **Voice-line detection for game audio.** Silero VAD separates speech from BGM in the captured audio and automatically snaps to it when you create an anki card or tap it.
- **Yomitan dictionaries render their embedded designs.** NOTE: You will need to re-load Yomitan dictionaries for this update. Structured content, images, and per-dictionary styling now display instead of being flattened to plain text, and definitions cross to Anki as real HTML. Plus a per-dictionary "Check for Updates" row and a source-language override for dictionaries that do not declare one.
- **Diagonal and slanted text.** *NOTE: Does not work with MeikiOCR! if you need angled text support, please switch to PaddleOCR or MLKit.* Angled dialogue and signage is detected, grouped, overlaid, and tappable at its true angle, furigana included.
- **Polish source language added**
- **Gamepad and keyboard control.** The capture sheet and the lens answer the dpad and sticks: left stick drags the panel edge, right stick scrolls everywhere in the app. Escape, arrows, and Enter mirror B, dpad, and A.
- **Translations are no longer fetched before you ask.** Capture defers the backend call until something needs the result, and History can hold back the answer until you tap the row.

### Fixes in 3.1.0

- Launch crash-loop on MuMu Player''s Android 12 image when Bergamot offline models are installed
- Arabic overlays now position correctly when the system language is set to Arabic
